<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Teusina</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1595">1595</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Treaty of Tyavzino · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russo-swedish-war-1590-1595">Russo-Swedish War (1590–1595)</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Teusina was signed on 18 May 1595 at Teusina, near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivangorod">Ivangorod</a>, ending the Russo-Swedish War of 1590–1595. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> recognised Swedish possession of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonia">Estonia</a>, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/narva">Narva</a>, while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> returned the fortress and district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kexholm">Kexholm</a> to Russia. The treaty also set out a border between the two states in the far north.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-teusina.jpg" alt="Treaty of Teusina" width="320" height="452" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ximfel1 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Border_changes_in_Finland_1595.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
